more than 24 hours later and the details  are still  jarring five experienced cyclists hit  and killed by a passing truck the  deadliest bike  car crash in southern nevada in 16 years  this happened yesterday morning on u.s  95 near searchlight  nevada highway patrol says a box truck  drifted into a group of about  20 cyclists they were on an annual ride  from the m resort looping through the  south  from boulder city to california and then  back up to henderson  a cyclist who knew many of the riders  involved says this crash  underscores the dangers they face as  they ride through southern nevada  i'm just really saddened by all this and  the more i think about it  i i really just hope that people will  pay more attention when they're out  there on the road  a vigil is planned for tomorrow at las  vegas cyclery in the southwest valley  the store's manager says his friends are  among those killed  we're a tight-knit group here in town it  affects all of us as cyclists  personally you know we're all out there  every day you know enjoying our hobby  and and trying to  you know stay alive it sounds like  everybody was doing the right thing  everybody was they had a vehicle with  them maintaining a safe  distance you know they were using lights  they were on a ride in a route that they  had used before  the driver of that box truck stayed at  the scene of the crash  nevada highway patrol says he did not  show signs of impairment
 

